<%# locals: (glance:, playthrough:) %>
<%# EVERY GOAL IS MET: END THE STORY HERE?

    THE WORDS ARE THE ENGINE'S. The heading, the goals and the question are
    `Playthrough::Glance#ending_offer`, read back as the engine wrote them; the
    two button labels are its `end` and `not_yet`. Nothing here is generated and
    nothing here decides anything: the outcome was fixed by the line that met
    the last beat, so which button is pressed, and when, cannot change which
    ending is reached.

    THE BATTLE PANEL'S FRAME AND BUTTON ROW (`playthroughs/_battle`). "End the
    story" posts the engine's own line (`end_line`, `/end`) to the same
    `turns#create` the text box reaches, so typing `/end` is the identical turn.
    "Not yet" withdraws the question (`TurnsController#put_off_ending`), and any
    typed line does too, by the engine's rule.

    ONCE THE QUESTION IS GONE AND THE ENDING IS STILL DUE, one standing button
    -- the same `/end` -- so the player can end the story whenever they choose. %>
<% if (offer = glance.ending_offer) %>
  <div class="sheet ending-offer">
    <p class="sheet-lead"><%= offer.heading %></p>
    <ul class="sheet-goals">
      <% offer.goals.each do |goal| %>
        <li><%= goal %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="sheet-prompt"><%= offer.question %></h3>
    <div class="sheet-actions">
      <%= form_with url: playthrough_turns_path(playthrough) do |form| %>
        <%= render "turns/request_token", token: SecureRandom.uuid %>
        <%= form.hidden_field :command, value: offer.end_line, id: nil %>
        <%= form.submit offer.end %>
      <% end %>
      <%= form_with url: put_off_ending_playthrough_turns_path(playthrough) do |form| %>
        <%= form.submit offer.not_yet %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% elsif glance.ending_due? %>
  <div class="sheet-actions ending-due">
    <%= form_with url: playthrough_turns_path(playthrough) do |form| %>
      <%= render "turns/request_token", token: SecureRandom.uuid %>
      <%= form.hidden_field :command, value: "/end", id: nil %>
      <%= form.submit "End the story" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
